--TEST--
`Core\Http\TlsInfo` answers the peer's own text as `tainted` and what the handshake settled as plain values, so a `string` binding takes the version and refuses the subject — `rule:security/tainted-sources`, `rule:http-server/a-reply-reports-its-tls-session`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The claim is *agreement*: one question asked of all seven members of
// `Core\Http\TlsInfo`, which is which side of the connection chose the answer. A version and a cipher are
// values out of a closed set this end offered, a `verified` is this process's
// own reading of its own policy, and a subject, an issuer and a chain are bytes
// the other end wrote into a certificate — verifying a chain settles which host
// answered and says nothing about what is written inside it.
Core\Http\Response $r = Core\Http\Client::get("https://api.example.com/thing");
var $info = $r->tls();
if ($info != null) {
    // Accepted: what the handshake settled carries no qualifier.
    string $version = $info->version();
    string $cipher = $info->cipher();
    bool $verified = $info->verified();
    echo $version, " ", $cipher, " ", $verified ? "verified" : "relaxed", "\n";

    // Accepted: the certificate's own text is where it can be held, and an
    // expiry is a `Core\Time\Instant` rather than text at all — a date is not
    // something a sink can misread.
    tainted string $subject = $info->subject();
    tainted string $issuer = $info->issuer();
    echo $subject, " ", $issuer, " ", $info->expiry()->toIso(), "\n";
    foreach ($info->peerChain() as tainted string $pem) {
        echo Core\Str::length($pem), "\n";
    }

    // Refused: narrowing through an assignment is the one direction the
    // qualifier never goes, and a peer's certificate has no launderer to put in
    // front of it.
    string $name = $info->subject();
    echo $name, "\n";
}
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `string`, found `tainted string`
   --> case.nvs:30:20
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
